From 24967ec7b1524eb258a7fa777b983ff2e856d4ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:20:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Input: bind scroll-wheel detents as virtual pointer buttons

Each wheel detent runs the bindings of a virtual button, WHEEL_UP,
WHEEL_DOWN, WHEEL_LEFT or WHEEL_RIGHT in ion.constants.pointer_buttons,
so they bind through MatchPointer like any other button:

    km.items.new(MatchPointer(btn.WHEEL_DOWN, logo=True), op)

A detent runs Press bindings, then Click bindings (MatchPointer's
default action) when no Press binding ran; it has no release, drag or
double click. High-resolution wheels add up their fractions of a detent.
An axis whose direction is bound is withheld from the client, unless the
binding passes through. Continuous (touchpad) scroll is unchanged.
